cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below.
title: "yutsis: optimal-form reduction of angular-momentum recoupling
  graphs with machine-verified phases"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Keller
    given-names: Karl
version: 0.11.1
date-released: "2026-08-16"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Karl-Keller/yutsis"
keywords:
  - angular momentum
  - Yutsis graphs
  - recoupling coefficients
  - 6j symbol
  - 9j symbol
  - Racah algebra
  - A* search
  - symbolic computation
  - quantum circuits
  - Schur transform
abstract: >-
  A solver for the optimal reduction of closed angular-momentum
  diagrams (Yutsis graphs) to summation formulae over Wigner 6j
  symbols, using A* search with admissible physics-derived heuristics,
  nauty-canonicalized states, and cycle-targeted rewrite moves. A
  symbolic phase engine derives exact signs for every move, and all
  emitted formulas are validated against two independent numerical
  oracles: brute-force magnetic-quantum-number summation of the closed
  diagram, and overlaps of explicitly constructed Clebsch-Gordan
  coupled states. Includes a compiler from pairs of angular-momentum
  coupling trees to verified elementary recoupling unitaries (the
  quantum Schur-transform gate family). Continues the reduction-
  ordering problem studied heuristically by NJGRAF and GYutsis, first
  attacked as an AI search problem in 1983.
